  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've refunded $14.00, the full price of the veggie burrito, to your Visa ending in 4242. You should see it within 3\u20135 business days. Sorry they sent you a chicken burrito instead.\n\nYou might also see a $31.52 hold from when you placed the order. That's not a second charge. It was released when the real charge went through and should disappear from your statement within 1\u20133 business days.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, thanks. I'll watch for the $14 to show up. Honestly though, this isn't the first problem I've had with orders lately. Over the past couple of months a few have gone wrong. Is anything being done about that, or is it just one-off refunds every time?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "That's a fair question, and I'm sorry it keeps happening. I can see the earlier issues on your account: a missing item in September and a wrong side last week. Having that happen again and again is frustrating.\n\nHere's how it works on my end. Every problem you report is recorded on your account and against the restaurant's order, so it's all on file. But I can only fix each order as it comes up. I don't have a tool to start a review of a restaurant or your order history, and I can't promise any changes on that side.\n\nTwo things that may help:\n- **Report problems soon after delivery.** Wrong or missing items need to be reported within 48 hours, and that also keeps the records accurate.\n- **Ask for a person if you want to raise it further.** If you'd like to talk to someone about the pattern, I can pass your case to a support specialist. They'll get back to you within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll do, but they'll see the full history.\n\nWould you like me to pass it on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yeah, go ahead and pass it on. I'd like someone to actually look at the pattern, not just refund each one. Also, you said the account needs a review. Why? I'm not sure what that means."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "escalate_to_human",
   "args": {
    "customer_id": "E302",
    "order_id": "K-8201",
    "reason": "customer_request",
    "summary": "Customer asked to speak with a person about repeated order problems. Today: order K-8201 (Taqueria Luz) came with a chicken burrito instead of the veggie burrito he ordered; $14.00 refunded to his card (RF-4000). Earlier issues: missing item on K-7012 (Sep 23, $9.00 support refund) and wrong side on K-7511 (Oct 15, $6.25 support refund, ticket TK-1144). He wants someone to look at the pattern rather than refunding each problem separately. No compensation is pending; the issue on this order is resolved."
   },
   "result": {
    "escalation_id": "ESC-700",
    "follow_up": "within 24 hours"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've passed your case to a support specialist (reference ESC-700). They'll contact you within 24 hours. I gave them today's wrong burrito plus the September and October issues, and said you'd like someone to look at the pattern rather than handle each order separately. I can't promise what they'll do, but they'll have the full history.\n\nAbout the \"review\": sorry for the confusion. I didn't mean your account is under review, and it isn't. There's nothing wrong with your account and nothing you need to do. When I said \"on file,\" I meant the issues are logged on your orders, and \"pass your case\" meant sending it to a specialist like I just did.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with tonight?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, that makes sense. So the account isn't under review, I just wanted someone to look at the pattern. Thanks for passing it on, I'll wait to hear from them."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "That's right. Your account isn't under review. The specialist will just look at the pattern you asked about.\n\nTo sum up:\n- **$14.00 refund** for the burrito is on its way to your Visa ending in 4242 and should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n- **The $31.52 hold** will drop off your statement in 1\u20133 business days. It's not an extra charge.\n- **A specialist** will contact you within 24 hours about the repeated problems (reference ESC-700).\n\nSorry again about the mix-up, Tom. I hope your next order goes smoothly!"
  }
